---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import quickQactions from "../../images/study sets/iphone/framed-18-pro/all-sets.png";
import iPadPhysics from "../../images/study sets/ipad/framed-m5/solar-system.png";
import iPadMusic from "../../images/study sets/ipad/framed-m5/music.png";
import iPhoneMusicDark from "../../images/study sets/iphone/framed-18-pro/music-dark.png";
import swipeYay from "../../images/study sets/iphone/framed-18-pro/study-swipes-dark.png";
---

<style>
  .text-primary-red {
    color: #fe2c55;
  }
</style>

<div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto grid gap-4">
  <div>
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-primary-red">Native Design</h2>
      <p class="text-lg">
        Study Sets is built entirely with native iOS design, so it looks right
        at home on both iPhone and iPad. Sidebars, sheets, and controls work
        the way you already expect them to.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 1/2, 1/2 -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <!-- Left -->
      <div
        class="bg-gradient-to-bl from-[#eaa8a8] to-[#fe2c55] p-6 rounded-2xl min-h-96 flex flex-col text-white"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Made for iPhone and iPad</h3>
        <div class="flex-grow flex items-center">
          <p>
            Study Sets uses the same navigation and controls as the rest of iOS,
            so there's nothing new to learn. Open it on whichever device is in
            reach and start studying.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right -->
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary-red">
          Add pictures to your cards
        </h3>
        <p class="text-base mt-4 mb-6">
          Cards aren't limited to text. Attach a picture to a term or
          definition and see it right in your deck, whether you're learning the
          planets or famous paintings. Tag your cards too, so you can find them
          later.
        </p>

        <div class="relative overflow-hidden w-full h-[50vh] min-h-[300px]">
          <Image
            src={iPadPhysics}
            alt="iPad displaying a deck of cards with pictures"
            class="absolute inset-0 object-cover transform origin-top-left translate-x-[5%] scale-[1.25]"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 5/12, 7/12 -->
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto grid gap-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-4">
      <!-- Left -->
      <div
        class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5 bg-white pt-6 px-6 rounded-2xl min-h-96 flex flex-col"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary-red">
          Everything at a glance.
        </h3>
        <p>
          Your favorite sets sit right at the top of All Sets, each with its own
          icon and color. Jump back into what you're studying in a single tap.
        </p>

        <div class="relative overflow-hidden w-full h-[70vh] min-h-[300px]">
          <Image
            src={quickQactions}
            alt="iPad displaying all sets sidebar"
            class="absolute inset-0 object-cover object-center-bottom px-6"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right -->
      <div
        class="col-span-12 md:col-span-7 bg-white pt-6 px-6 rounded-2xl flex flex-col justify-between h-full"
      >
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary-red">
            Listen to your Apple Music library
          </h3>
          <p class="mb-6">
            Study Sets has access to your Apple Music library. Without even
            leaving the app you can change songs to get you in the perfect
            study mood.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative overflow-hidden w-full h-[60vh] min-h-[300px] mt-auto"
        >
          <Image
            src={iPadMusic}
            alt="iPad displaying all sets sidebar"
            class="absolute inset-0 object-cover transform origin-top-left translate-x-[5%] scale-[1.25]"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 7/12, 5/12 -->
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto grid gap-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-12 gap-4">
      <div
        class="col-span-12 md:col-span-7 bg-black pt-6 px-6 rounded-2xl min-h-96 flex flex-col"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary-red">Beautiful Design</h3>
        <p class="text-white justify-left">
          Study Sets has a beautiful and elegant modern design- in both dark and
          light mode. You can even change the apps accent color.
        </p>

        <div class="relative overflow-hidden w-full h-[70vh] min-h-[300px]">
          <Image
            src={iPhoneMusicDark}
            alt="iPad displaying all sets sidebar"
            class="absolute inset-0 object-cover object-center-bottom px-6"
          />
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right -->
      <div
        class="col-span-12 md:col-span-5 bg-white pt-6 px-6 rounded-2xl min-h-96 flex flex-col"
      >
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-primary-red">Swipe Right</h3>
        <p>
          Quickly blow through study cards by swiping right if you get the
          answer and left if you didn't. Once you finish with the current deck
          you'll get a report on how you did. I bet it was fantastic.
        </p>

        <div class="relative overflow-hidden w-full h-[70vh] min-h-[300px]">
          <Image
            src={swipeYay}
            alt="iPad displaying all sets sidebar"
            class="absolute inset-0 object-cover object-center-bottom px-6"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
